;
; The tools' hints.
MSG_TOOL_FREEHAND (//)
Freehand: a line where the pointer goes
MSG_TOOL_DOTS (//)
Dotted freehand: the brush where the pointer is
MSG_TOOL_LINE (//)
Line: from where the button goes down to where it is let go
MSG_TOOL_CURVE (//)
Curve: a line, then pulled into a bend with a second press
MSG_TOOL_RECTANGLE (//)
Rectangle: from one corner to the other
MSG_TOOL_ELLIPSE (//)
Ellipse: in the box from one corner to the other
MSG_TOOL_POLYGON (//)
Polygon: a corner at each release, closed on the first corner
MSG_TOOL_FILL (//)
Fill: the area of one colour that is clicked
MSG_TOOL_AIRBRUSH (//)
Airbrush: a spray where the pointer is, for as long as it is held
MSG_TOOL_PICK (//)
Pick colour: the colour under the pointer
MSG_TOOL_TEXT (//)
Text: typed, and put where the picture is clicked
MSG_TOOL_GRAB (//)
Cut brush: a part of the picture taken as the brush
MSG_TOOL_HAND (//)
Hand: the picture moved with the pointer
MSG_FILLED_HINT (//)
Rectangles, ellipses and polygons filled
MSG_UNDO_HINT (//)
Undo the last change
MSG_REDO_HINT (//)
Make the change undone again
MSG_ZOOM_IN_HINT (//)
Show the picture larger
MSG_ZOOM_OUT_HINT (//)
Show the picture smaller
MSG_FIT_HINT (//)
Show the whole picture as large as it fits
MSG_SWAP_HINT (//)
Swap the two colours
;
; The zoom above the picture, in per cent.
MSG_ZOOM (//)
%ld %%
;
; The side panel's sections.
MSG_SECTION_BRUSH (//)
Brush
MSG_SECTION_COLOUR (//)
Colour
;
; The line under the picture: its size, the zoom and the brush, and
; while painting where the pointer is.
MSG_STATUS (//)
%ld x %ld   %ld:1   brush %ld
MSG_STATUS_AT (//)
%ld x %ld   %ld:1   brush %ld   at %ld, %ld
MSG_STATUS_OWN (//)
%ld x %ld   %ld:1   brush %ld x %ld
MSG_STATUS_OWN_AT (//)
%ld x %ld   %ld:1   brush %ld x %ld   at %ld, %ld
;
; The new picture's window.
MSG_NEW_TITLE (//)
New Picture
MSG_WIDTH (//)
Width
MSG_HEIGHT (//)
Height
MSG_OK (//)
OK
MSG_ABOUT (//)
Paint %s\n\nPictures in true colour, painted with\nbuilt-in and cut brushes.
MSG_CANCEL (//)
Cancel
;
; The text's window.
MSG_TEXT_TITLE (//)
Text
MSG_TEXT (//)
Text
MSG_FONT (//)
Font
MSG_FONT_TITLE (//)
The text's font
;
; Requesters.
MSG_CHANGED (//)
The picture has changed.\nSave it first?
MSG_CHANGED_BUTTONS (//)
Save|Don't save|Cancel
MSG_NO_PICTURE (//)
There is no memory for a picture\nof %ld by %ld pixels.
MSG_NO_UNDO (//)
That change was too large to keep:\nit cannot be undone.
MSG_NO_OWN_SCREEN (//)
No screen of its own could be opened.
MSG_NO_FONT (//)
The font could not be opened.
MSG_FILL_SHORT (//)
There was not memory enough to fill all of it.
MSG_OPEN_TITLE (//)
Open a picture
MSG_SAVE_AS_TITLE (//)
Save the picture as
MSG_NO_OPEN (//)
%s\ncannot be opened:\n%s
MSG_NO_SAVE (//)
The picture cannot be saved\nas %s:\n%s
MSG_NO_PART (//)
%s\ncannot be opened.
MSG_UNTITLED (//)
Untitled
MSG_OPEN_BRUSH_TITLE (//)
Open a brush
MSG_SAVE_BRUSH_TITLE (//)
Save the brush as
MSG_NO_SAVE_BRUSH (//)
The brush cannot be saved\nas %s:\n%s
MSG_BRUSH_TOO_LARGE (//)
A brush can be at most %ld by %ld pixels.
MSG_NO_BRUSH (//)
There is no memory for a brush\nof %ld by %ld pixels.
;
; What the shell is told.
MSG_NOLIBRARY (//)
No %s\n
MSG_NOSCREEN (//)
No screen - no display\n
MSG_NOMEMORY (//)
No memory for the window\n
MSG_BADSCREEN (//)
SCREEN is OWN or DESKTOP\n
